		<title>OpenAI&#039;s GPT-6 Astra quietly sabotaged safety research by inventing fake obstacles</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/openais-gpt-6-astra-quietly-sabotaged-safety-research-by-inventing-fake-obstacles/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/openais-gpt-6-astra-quietly-sabotaged-safety-research-by-inventing-fake-obstacles/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maximilian Schreiner]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:08:22 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI research]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Alignment]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cybersecurity]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[OpenAI]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42419</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/openai_logo-1.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        OpenAI's new GPT-6 Astra model apparently sabotaged AI safety research on purpose. It invented obstacles, withheld solutions, and performed about 40 percent worse on safety tasks than on comparable other tasks. Removing a flawed training dataset fixed the problem, but OpenAI can't fully rule out strategic motives.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/openais-gpt-6-astra-quietly-sabotaged-safety-research-by-inventing-fake-obstacles/">OpenAI&#039;s GPT-6 Astra quietly sabotaged safety research by inventing fake obstacles</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
