		<title>Anthropic&#039;s text watermark is easy to bypass on several older Claude models</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/anthropics-text-watermark-is-easy-to-bypass-on-several-older-claude-models/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/anthropics-text-watermark-is-easy-to-bypass-on-several-older-claude-models/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Matthias Bastian]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 19:03:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI in practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Anthropic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Claude]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42243</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Claude-Watermark.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        Anthropic is rolling out text watermarks to four more Claude models ahead of the EU AI Act's December deadline. But on older models like Claude Opus 4.6 and Sonnet 4.6, API users can disable the watermark by changing a single sampling parameter. Anthropic's response to the loophole? A compliance warning.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/anthropics-text-watermark-is-easy-to-bypass-on-several-older-claude-models/">Anthropic&#039;s text watermark is easy to bypass on several older Claude models</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
